    },
    {
      "claim": "Losartan, a related imidazole acid, shows an efflux ratio of 3.7 in Caco-2 (C215) and reduced efflux with P-gp inhibition (C177, C218), indicating intestinal efflux liability in this chemical class; however, losartan is a monoacid/tetrazole and less transferable to the query's bis-carboxylate.",
      "card_ids": ["C215", "C177", "C218"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Olmesartan free acid shows moderate Caco-2/SPIP permeability (C169, C219), but olmesartan is administered as the medoxomil prodrug and even the prodrug has only about 29% oral F (C116); this does not affirmatively support F >= 20% for the query free bis-acid.",
      "card_ids": ["C169", "C219", "C116"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The query is a dianion at pH 7.4 (neutral fraction 0, pKa 3.23/5.77) with logD 0.56, TPSA 92.42 and 10 rotatable bonds, consistent with low passive permeability; no direct query F or active-uptake evidence exists.",
