      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "contradictory",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C219"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct experimental F measurement for the query molecule.",
    "EXP3174 is a metabolite, not the query; structural differences (acrylic acid/thiophene side chain vs chloro/tetrazole-biphenyl) limit transferability.",
    "No query-specific permeability, solubility, or intestinal metabolism data.",
    "Olmesartan free-acid permeability is moderate, but its oral F is only measured as the prodrug; free-acid F is unknown.",
    "No information on active uptake or intestinal metabolism for the query.",
    "Caco-2/SPIP permeability is not a direct absolute bioavailability endpoint."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L5 adds EXP3174 poor-permeability confirmation (C199) and losartan efflux evidence (C215, C177, C218), strengthening the affirmative low-absorption case for the query's dianionic bis-acid imidazole scaffold. Olmesartan free-acid moderate permeability (C219) is less transferable and does not overturn the low prediction. Prediction remains low with low confidence."
}

